index cbc4a6381..9647b36a7 100644
--- a/broker/card/ASSUMPTIONS.md
+++ b/broker/card/ASSUMPTIONS.md
@@ -22,3 +22,4 @@ to change.
 | C14 | **Shown until confirmed, to the paired phone only.** "Show once" is read as: the page goes only to the phone that paired (Handler's `paired`), never cached (`no-store`), and is re-shown on reload until the confirm, since a reload would otherwise lose a card nobody holds yet. Wrong answers have no attempt limit: whoever can answer can already read the card. A cross-site POST (Origin of another host, or `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`) is refused. | HW-1, CH-7 | A one-shot view would need a re-generate path instead. |
 | C15 | **Confirm values.** One passphrase word and one recovery key group, positions drawn from the box's randomness, compared in constant time after the card's normalisation (case, spaces and dashes forgiven). Two values from different sheets prove the owner holds both the passphrase and the recovery sheet. | HW-1 | `Display.Confirm`. |
 | C16 | **The page.** Print is offered first, then save as a file (the bare sheet, `Content-Disposition: attachment`), with a warning not to take a screenshot or photo (phone cloud sync). The controls are hidden in print. After the confirm every request gets 410 saying no copy is kept and that a new card comes from rotation (REC-4). Journal events are fixed strings; `Card` and `Display` format as placeholders, so no stray log line carries card text. | HW-1, ONB-7, REC-4 | `display.go`. |
+| C17 | **Rotation mode (CTRL-card-rot).** `DisplayConfig.Rotate` makes the display show only the rotated parts (the rest blanked before rendering, the Wi-Fi name kept from `WiFiName`), titled as a rotation with "Until you confirm, your current card keeps working" and a cancel. The confirm asks a passphrase word and/or recovery key group of the new parts, or else one check value (Wi-Fi last four, setup code, grid check). `Discard` erases a waiting display for cancel or lapse (`ErrDiscard` from `Provision` does the same); once `Provision` reports `ErrInEffect` (part of the new card already written), the owner has just typed values back from their copy and the rotation is used up, so the display erases its copy as after a full confirm (`Confirmed` stays false), `Discard` returns `ErrInEffect`, and every later request gets 410 with the one step that finishes: keep the new card and the current one, and start a new card from the box page with the passphrase or recovery key from whichever card works. Not every part of the new card need be in effect (the Wi-Fi password, setup secret and grid are stored after the slots, and a failed recovery-key write leaves the old key in effect), so the text never says to use the new card alone; the next rotation must replace every part this one rotated (recovery R14) (CH-12; #1090 review F1, F3). | REC-4, HW-1 | `display.go`, `render.go`. |
